WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.769 --> 00:00:15.933
Meg and John had a long engagement—three years to be exact— since her parents, though they accepted John

2
00:00:15.993 --> 00:00:20.916
as their future son-in-law, wished the couple to wait until Meg turned twenty before they married.

3
00:00:21.977 --> 00:00:26.520
Now Meg was old enough, and the happy but eager couple were free to take their vows.

4
00:00:28.448 --> 00:00:31.109
"Can you believe that in one month I shall be Mrs.

5
00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:31.929
John Brookes?"

6
00:00:32.609 --> 00:00:37.051
Meg gushed to her fiance one glorious spring day as they took a walk around the Laurence garden.

7
00:00:37.071 --> 00:00:43.092
"I wish it were today, this moment," John said tenderly as he wrapped his arm around her waist.

8
00:00:44.433 --> 00:00:50.034
During the three years of their engagement, Meg had grown from a sweet, mild-mannered girl into a capable,

9
00:00:50.114 --> 00:00:51.135
beautiful, young woman.

10
00:00:51.155 --> 00:00:58.361
"Well, I don't," Meg said very unromantically, "because there is so much to do, I don't have a

11
00:00:58.421 --> 00:01:01.842
moment to spare if I am going to get everything ready before we get married."

12
00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:08.323
So John patiently listened as his soon-to-be bride told him about the countless number of things that needed

13
00:01:08.383 --> 00:01:09.924
to be done before their wedding day.

14
00:01:10.884 --> 00:01:15.585
One person who still prayed that the wedding day would never come was Jo who, despite the past

15
00:01:15.626 --> 00:01:19.467
three years, refused to accept that Meg would become a wife very soon.

16
00:01:20.927 --> 00:01:22.027
"Look at those two!

17
00:01:22.527 --> 00:01:28.967
It's rather disgusting, it is," Jo mumbled miserably as she spied on her sister and Brookes from the

18
00:01:29.027 --> 00:01:30.088
safety of the March home.

19
00:01:31.369 --> 00:01:36.413
Jabbing more of the air than the potato she was supposed to be peeling, Jo carelessly tossed the

20
00:01:36.453 --> 00:01:41.517
vegetable into a basket of half-peeled other ones that she had butchered while watching Meg and Brookes wander

21
00:01:41.537 --> 00:01:42.638
through the Laurences' garden.

22
00:01:42.658 --> 00:01:47.021
"Jo? Are you done with the potatoes yet?"

23
00:01:47.341 --> 00:01:50.784
Beth asked as she and Amy walked into the kitchen wearing aprons.

24
00:01:51.792 --> 00:01:55.214
It was clear that the other girls had also changed in the past three years.

25
00:01:56.074 --> 00:02:00.376
Jo, who had long thick hair again, had pulled it into a neat, ladylike bun.

26
00:02:00.876 --> 00:02:05.258
Her face had softened, and she seemed calmer, more comfortable with herself and her body.

27
00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:11.361
Beth was a little taller, though very thin and without the glow of health that her sisters had.

28
00:02:12.081 --> 00:02:16.703
Still, she always wore a smile on her face and never held back from saying a kind word

29
00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.424
or performing a good deed for others.

30
00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:21.562
But the most remarkable change was in Amy.

31
00:02:23.504 --> 00:02:28.227
She had always been pretty, but now she had turned into the kind of stunning beauty that artists

32
00:02:28.287 --> 00:02:35.033
dream about painting, poets are inspired to create poems for, and singers are moved to write songs about.

33
00:02:36.294 --> 00:02:42.799
All traces of the old Amy, including her tantrums and whining, were replaced by a sophisticated, polished, well-mannered

34
00:02:42.839 --> 00:02:43.260
young woman.

35
00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:53.464
"Jo! You've stripped half the peel off this innocent vegetable and turned it into some modern art sculpture!"

36
00:02:54.425 --> 00:02:59.649
Amy picked up a battered potato, part of its peel dangling loosely, as Beth giggled and picked up

37
00:02:59.709 --> 00:03:01.110
some others in similar shape.

38
00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:06.253
"Huh?" Jo tore her eyes away from the window to see what Amy was talking about.

39
00:03:06.273 --> 00:03:14.279
"We'd better decide upon an alternative for the potato pancakes then," sighed Amy, wrinkling her perfect forehead at

40
00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:14.819
her sister.

41
00:03:16.508 --> 00:03:17.929
"It's all their fault!"

42
00:03:18.409 --> 00:03:23.471
Jo pointed accusingly at Meg and John far off in the distance, unaware that they were being blamed

43
00:03:23.491 --> 00:03:24.692
for the state of the potatoes.

44
00:03:24.712 --> 00:03:29.974
"Oh, Jo," Amy remarked, shaking her head as she left the kitchen.

45
00:03:31.274 --> 00:03:35.736
Beth stood for a moment with Jo, wishing she could erase the pain on her sister's face and

46
00:03:35.756 --> 00:03:36.897
the deeper one in her heart.

47
00:03:36.917 --> 00:03:42.639
"As much as we'd like it, nothing stays the same, Jo," she said softly.

48
00:03:42.659 --> 00:03:46.414
"Letting go of something doesn't mean you're going to lose it.

49
00:03:47.314 --> 00:03:52.419
It means you are allowing it to find another home," she added with wisdom beyond her years.

50
00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:57.784
For Jo, Beth's words rang true in so many ways, not only concerning Meg.

51
00:03:58.745 --> 00:04:02.889
Aunt March had taken such a fancy to Amy during the brief time she stayed with her while

52
00:04:02.949 --> 00:04:07.913
Beth was sick, that the old lady had replaced Jo with Amy as her companion.

53
00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:14.105
At first Jo was upset, but then she decided to view the matter positively and chose to use

54
00:04:14.145 --> 00:04:16.486
her time wisely by focusing on her writing.

55
00:04:16.506 --> 00:04:19.748
"Is Laurie coming home this weekend?"

56
00:04:20.128 --> 00:04:25.870
asked Amy, tying her wavy blonde hair back in a green ribbon that matched her dress as she

57
00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.531
got ready to go to Aunt March's the next morning.

58
00:04:29.452 --> 00:04:32.913
"I hope not, but I wouldn't be surprised," Jo answered.

59
00:04:33.794 --> 00:04:38.856
She knew that although Laurie was away now at college, he insisted on coming home every week to,

60
00:04:38.916 --> 00:04:41.457
as he said, "get away from those horrid books."

61
00:04:42.877 --> 00:04:47.679
"Well, he's promised to escort me and Aunt March to the theater and she's hoping it will be

62
00:04:47.739 --> 00:04:49.319
this Saturday," said Amy.

63
00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:56.922
Yawning, uninterested in the trivial worries of Aunt March's life, Jo flipped through her book and replied sarcastically,

64
00:04:56.942 --> 00:05:03.104
"I'm certain that Laurie will be thrilled to oblige Aunt March's every wish."

65
00:05:04.396 --> 00:05:10.040
Thankfully some things hadn't changed, such as Jo's passion for writing and her favorite spot to do it

66
00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:16.725
in. Armed with her pen, Jo sat upstairs in her sanctuary, her hand flying over the paper as

67
00:05:16.745 --> 00:05:20.287
she tried to finish another chapter in the novel she was currently working on.

68
00:05:21.368 --> 00:05:26.311
With the confidence she gained from selling some of her short stories, Jo decided to move on to

69
00:05:26.371 --> 00:05:27.512
longer pieces of writing.

70
00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:32.956
She was about to complete the last page when someone knocked at her door.

71
00:05:34.148 --> 00:05:39.172
"Whoever it is had better go away," Jo called out threateningly, as she refused to get up to

72
00:05:39.232 --> 00:05:39.952
see who it was.

73
00:05:41.093 --> 00:05:46.376
The knocker persisted, this time with a series of short taps in the rhythm of a well-known children's

74
00:05:46.417 --> 00:05:48.738
song. "Argh!"

75
00:05:49.058 --> 00:05:53.501
Jo threw her pen across the room and stomped over to unlock the door and unleash her fury.

76
00:05:53.521 --> 00:06:00.846
"Surprise!" Laurie shoved his face in as soon as the door was unlocked and tackled Jo with such

77
00:06:00.906 --> 00:06:03.048
a hug that she didn't have a chance to react.

78
00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:09.505
Laurie, now twenty, the same age as Meg, had indeed blossomed into a handsome young man.

79
00:06:10.846 --> 00:06:16.411
He was very tall with broad shoulders and wavy dark hair that constantly fell over his left eye,

80
00:06:16.671 --> 00:06:18.533
giving him a very romantic look.

81
00:06:19.474 --> 00:06:24.218
Many girls at his college worshipped him as if he were a Roman god, and Laurie did not

82
00:06:24.278 --> 00:06:25.539
discourage their attention.

83
00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:32.284
However, to Jo and the girls, he was still silly Laurie, which he did not mind, because he

84
00:06:32.304 --> 00:06:34.246
could comfortably be himself around them.

85
00:06:34.266 --> 00:06:38.328
"Do they not teach you to read in college?"

86
00:06:38.708 --> 00:06:44.251
Jo asked, pointing to the sign she had hung on the door that read: Interrupt At Own Risk.

87
00:06:44.952 --> 00:06:48.954
Shrugging his shoulders, Laurie swung a brown bag in front of Jo's face.

88
00:06:49.775 --> 00:06:52.336
"You don't want to be interrupted even for this?"

89
00:06:52.776 --> 00:06:53.317
he teased.

90
00:06:53.337 --> 00:06:55.118
"Oh, Laurie!

91
00:06:55.658 --> 00:06:56.339
Thank you!"

92
00:06:56.779 --> 00:06:58.580
Jo snatched the bag from his hand.

93
00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:06.382
Like a hungry lion, she nearly ripped the bag open and shoved two candies into her mouth, sucking

94
00:07:06.562 --> 00:07:09.823
one in each cheek, making her look like an overgrown chipmunk.

95
00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:16.064
Meg had put all the girls on a diet before the wedding, forbidding any sweets in the house.

96
00:07:17.025 --> 00:07:21.606
Jo seldom had cravings, but candies were something she could not live without.

97
00:07:22.426 --> 00:07:27.667
Thanking Laurie for sharing the forbidden treats, Jo was glad to have him to rely on when things

98
00:07:27.788 --> 00:07:28.408
got tough.
